  "provider_query": "Node.js 22.0.0 GitHub release page",
  "answer": "The Node.js **v22.0.0** GitHub release page is here:\n\n**https://github.com/nodejs/node/releases/tag/v22.0.0**\n\nReleased 24 Apr 2024 by RafaelGSS (with @marco-ippolito). It was the “Current” line at the time (LTS later). Highlights include `require()` of ESM graphs, a WebSocket client, and a V8 update.\n\n### Related results\n\n1. **GitHub release tag (primary)** — https://github.com/nodejs/node/releases/tag/v22.0.0 — Official v22.0.0 notes, signature, and commits. [[1]](https://github.com/nodejs/node/releases/tag/v22.0.0)\n\n2. **nodejs.org blog source for the same release** — https://github.com/nodejs/nodejs.org/blob/main/apps/site/pages/en/blog/release/v22.0.0.md — Blog markdown with download links and SHASUMS. [[2]](https://github.com/nodejs/nodejs.org/blob/main/apps/site/pages/en/blog/release/v22.0.0.md)\n\n3. **Binary download index for v22.0.0** — https://nodejs.org/download/release/v22.0.0/ — Installers and tarballs for that exact version. [[3]](https://nodejs.org/download/release/v22.0.0)\n\n4. **Node.js 22 changelog (repo)** — https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/main/doc/changelogs/CHANGELOG_V22.md — Full 22.x changelog, starting from 22.0.0. [[4]](https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/main/doc/changelogs/CHANGELOG_V22.md)\n\n5. **Raw changelog** — https://github.com/nodejs/node/raw/main/doc/changelogs/CHANGELOG_V22.md — Same changelog as plain text. [[5]](https://github.com/nodejs/node/raw/main/doc/changelogs/CHANGELOG_V22.md)\n\n6. **All nodejs/node releases** — https://github.com/nodejs/node/releases — Release list (v22.0.0 is historical; later 22.x tags are further down). [[6]](https://github.com/nodejs/node/releases)\n\n7. **Tags list** — https://github.com/nodejs/node/tags — Signed tags, including later v22.x. [[7]](https://github.com/nodejs/node/tags)\n\n8. **Support timeline** — https://endoflife.date/nodejs — Node.js 22 released 24 Apr 2024; security support through 30 Apr 2027 on that page. [[8]](https://endoflife.date/nodejs)",
